WEBVTT

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.380
Senko Educational Films presents one of a series of six films

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.830
dealing with the subject of nuclear radiation.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.820
Fallout is a vitally important subject.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:10.720
Bombs are being tested which to some extent contaminate the atmosphere.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.690
It is only natural that we ask ourselves what is the extent of such contamination

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.720
and what are the possible results.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.740
The release of atomic energy is always accompanied by certain invisible but powerful radiation.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:39.540
nuclear radiation, radiations which can be dangerous. Every time it rains, it rains radioactive

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:47.660
particles which are in the atmosphere because of the testing of nuclear weapons. As a result,

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:57.500
all of us acquire radioactivity through the food we eat and drink. There has always been

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.880
and some nuclear radiation in our environment.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.570
Such background radiation is usually quite small, and it comes from two principal sources.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:15.390
Naturally radioactive substances, such as uranium and radium, which are found in rocks and soil,

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:23.320
and cosmic radiations, so named because they are thought to be produced beyond the Earth's atmosphere.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.200
Some cosmic rays are absorbed by the atmosphere.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.860
but an appreciable amount does get through and consequently has an effect on living things.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:44.650
Cosmic rays change part of the atmospheric nitrogen-14 to radioactive carbon-14.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:52.530
Carbon-14, in the form of carbon dioxide, enters all growing plants during photosynthesis.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.360
We use many of these plants for food.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.980
Other plants are eaten by animals which are...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:09.940
are in turn eaten by man thus naturally occurring radioactive atoms are found within all living

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:18.560
plants and animals every living thing is exposed to its own internal radiation as well as to

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:27.330
radiation from the external background in the more industrially advanced countries such as ours

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.920
most people have also been exposed.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.330
to man-made radiations from medical and dental x-rays. The average person in the United States

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:44.520
receives roughly the same amount of radiation from x-ray and fluoroscopic examinations as he does

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:51.460
from natural background radiation. The danger from the amounts of radiations thus received is thought

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:59.040
to be relatively slight. However, two important facts should be clearly understood. Number one,

00:03:59.350 --> 00:03:59.970
Radiation.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.900
effects on living cells.

00:04:02.172 --> 00:04:03.172
are cumulative.

00:04:03.804 --> 00:04:05.964
They add up over a period of time.

00:04:06.684 --> 00:04:07.404
Number two.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.940
Most scientists would say that there is no minimum level of radiation

00:04:12.956 --> 00:04:15.316
below which no damage will be done.

00:04:19.772 --> 00:04:24.532
In recent years, the general public has become increasingly aware of the dangers from yet

00:04:24.532 --> 00:04:26.272
another source of radiation.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:27.720
fallout.

00:04:28.156 --> 00:04:29.996
from atomic explosions.

00:04:30.764 --> 00:04:37.124
Every nuclear or thermonuclear bomb throws into the air a large cloud of radioactive particles.

00:04:38.284 --> 00:04:42.944
These man-made radioisotopes remain aloft for varying periods of time.

00:04:43.372 --> 00:04:44.612
But most of them...

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.444
eventually returned to Earth.

00:04:47.372 --> 00:04:48.732
It is this return.

00:04:49.292 --> 00:04:50.452
which is known as

00:04:50.828 --> 00:04:51.328
fallout.

00:04:53.324 --> 00:04:56.564
To simplify study of its distribution patterns,

00:04:56.908 --> 00:04:59.708
Fallout has been divided into three classes.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:09.860
local, intermediate, and delayed. Local or close-in fallout consists of the heaviest particles.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:14.960
This type of fallout is also known as atmospheric fallout.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.800
because the particles do not rise above the lower layers of the Earth's atmosphere.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:24.500
Their fallout distribution is affected by the local wind patterns.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.980
Atmospheric fallout is almost always...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.480
restricted to the immediate area of the explosion. It usually falls within a

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:40.720
period of one day and seldom farther than a few hundred miles from ground to zero.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.510
Intermediate fallout is composed of much lighter particles.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:57.060
Most of these enter into the troposphere at altitudes between 35,000 and 55,000 feet.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.980
Tropospheric fallout would...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:07.320
descend very slowly if it were pulled down only by gravity. Actually, it descends within a few

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:13.080
weeks after the explosion because most of it is washed out of the air by rain and snow.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.960
Radioactive particles in the troposphere are carried around the world by prevailing winds

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.440
and may spread over large areas of the Earth.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:29.670
However, it is possible for this type of fallout to be concentrated in small areas

00:06:30.316 --> 00:06:32.316
If there is heavy rainfall,

00:06:32.364 --> 00:06:34.524
while the radioactive cloud is overhead.

00:06:38.092 --> 00:06:39.332
The third type,

00:06:39.788 --> 00:06:42.108
Delayed or stratospheric fallout.

00:06:42.796 --> 00:06:44.716
may remain in the air for months.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.084
or even years.

00:06:47.404 --> 00:06:53.164
Meteorologists are attempting to learn more about the interchange of air between the stratosphere...

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.260
and the lower layers.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:57.340
At the present time, however,

00:06:57.708 --> 00:06:59.988
They do not have sufficient information to

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:07.410
predict exactly how long before the radioactive particles will fall or where they are likely to

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:14.970
descend. Recent developments in the miniaturization of electronic components have made it possible

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:20.900
it possible to send many information gathering devices high above the earth. These include

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:27.370
radiation detectors which measure the amount and kinds of radiation present at various

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:28.470
altitudes. Then,

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.140
these findings are radioed back to Earth.

00:07:33.836 --> 00:07:37.836
Exploratory balloons are also used to chart air currents.

00:07:39.564 --> 00:07:41.404
Thus, we have a clearer picture.

00:07:41.868 --> 00:07:44.268
of probable fallout distribution.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.980
Our principal interest in radioactive fallout

00:07:49.324 --> 00:07:52.624
concerns the possible danger of biological damage.

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:54.772
Will it hurt people?

00:07:55.756 --> 00:07:56.816
And if so,

00:07:57.452 --> 00:07:58.432
In what ways?

00:07:58.924 --> 00:07:59.784
And how much?

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:05.410
For a moment, let's review the main principal types of radiation.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:12.960
Alpha particles have a relatively high mass, but their penetrating power is very slight.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.540
Alpha particles are easily stopped by a single sheet of paper.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.980
They will not readily penetrate human skin.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:27.670
However, alpha particle emitters are dangerous if they enter the human body, as in food.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.930
particles are somewhat more penetrating. Their mass is much smaller, but their velocity is

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:42.140
greater. Their penetrating power is such that it takes several sheets of paper or a thin sheet

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:49.240
of aluminum to stop them. Still, as in the case of alpha particles, betas from radioisotopes must

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:57.610
actually be emitted inside the body before any great damage can be done. Gamma rays, which are

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:59.330
are similar in character to x-rays,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:07.620
are very penetrating gamma radiations can be stopped only by massive shielding they are

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:16.250
extremely dangerous from outside the body as well as from within radioactive fallout includes

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:28.430
radioisotopes which emit all three alpha particles beta particles and gamma rays fortunately most of

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.970
isotopes formed by the

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:37.550
explosion of atomic devices have short half-lives. The total level of radioactivity caused by fallout

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:46.310
fades quite rapidly. However, some bomb debris remains active for many years. It is the build-up

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:53.990
of these products which is the cause for our concern. The long-term fallout problem particularly

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:59.980
involves strontium-90, cesium-137, and carbon-40.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:08.030
Strontium-90, because of a unique combination of properties, probably represents the greatest danger.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.600
It is one of the more abundant fission products.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:19.760
Strontium-90 has a half-life of 25 years and is a relatively strong source of radiation.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:25.290
Much of the Strontium-90 is carried up into the stratosphere.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:29.720
It spreads over the whole Earth and is gradually deposited.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.920
during a period of years.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:38.280
At the present time, Strontium-90 is not considered a serious threat,

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:43.920
but the creation of additional radioactive fallout may cause it to become one.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:52.230
We do know that Strontium-90 has caused bone tumors in animals under experimental conditions.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:59.900
The question of permissible radiation dosage in humans remains the all-important consideration.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:08.430
When we stop to consider that all living matter has always been exposed to some amount of background radiation,

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:14.860
it becomes evident that relatively small amounts do not cause significant damage.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:22.520
Most of our knowledge about radiation damage has been obtained from work done with animals in the laboratory.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:27.900
But we have learned a great deal about the kinds of damage which may occur.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:29.980
The data we...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.020
have indicate that the effects of radiation in human beings are similar to those found in animals.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:41.560
The importance of controlling the amount of radiation to which we are exposed

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:48.410
is emphasized by the fact that people who work with atomic energy are required to wear radiation

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:56.840
measuring devices. Careful records of the readings are kept. These records help to keep the workers

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.880
from receiving dangerous dosages.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:08.630
When radiating waves or particles pass through a substance, some of them bump into molecules.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:14.940
And this is serious because of the delicate balance within a living cell.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:19.910
Each molecule must be just what it is.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:28.040
Any chemical change, however slight, may substantially change the normal life processes or even kill the cell.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:37.690
every living cell contains a collection of tiny units called genes. Taken together, the genes

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:43.230
determine the characteristics with which an individual is born. The inheritance mechanism

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:50.520
is particularly sensitive to radiation. This has given rise to much concern about radiation-induced

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:58.490
genetic mutation. The reduplication of genetic patterns is not eternally static.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:06.190
Every so often, a gene changes or mutates, and a characteristic of the organism is altered.

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:15.690
We do not know the exact process by which mutations occur, but we do know that they can be caused by radiation.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:22.760
Once changed, the new form of the gene is passed on as faithfully as the old one was.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:29.980
The results of genetic mutation are almost invariably undesirable.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:37.180
Any radiation dose, however small, can produce mutations.

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:41.800
The number of them is in direct proportion to the amount of radiation.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:50.080
Presently existing evidence indicates that fallout has caused only a small increase in background radiation

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:55.140
and correspondingly, only a minute increase in mutations.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:59.980
We have discussed some of the...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:07.500
major aspects of radioactive fallout. The fallout question is controversial. Perhaps the only

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:13.790
positive statement we can make is that we have so far found no beneficial effect of penetrating

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:21.200
radiation on healthy living matter. On the other hand, we have not observed any significant effect

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:28.520
on the health and well-being of the human race as a whole. So the studies of radioactive fallout

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.970
remain in concern.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:39.370
inclusive. Much has been and is being done in an attempt to solve the many problems involved.

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:48.100
But this we know. Mankind needs to proceed with caution, knowing that only the future

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:51.990
will produce scientifically acceptable answers.
